{"kind":"report","text":"Approved: exact CUT-A head ce93a51c72051693c8c615946372270e0ddaff5a on builder/cut-a-register-values-20261114, all 22 artifacts, for request 5b28b7ac under implementation promise f3c4b383 and my promise 8445ea9a. The helper changes one Worker's register settings and nothing else. The failed gate stays failed, and its isolated repair and follow-up meet the rule of `docs/evidence-filing.md`, \"Follow-up after a gate\".\n\nThe gate and its follow-up:\n\n- Gate attempt 1 at 554187d4, tree 7f7e180f, wrote exit 1. Plain reports 76 failed, 4,540 passed and one skipped, with one failed file, `examples/repo-in-ai/test/hosted-loop.test.ts`. Native never ran.\n- From 554187d4 to the head, only that test file, the note and three manifests change. Repair d19e9453 changes the test file alone. No other source imports it; `hosted-loop/agent.ts:4` names it only in a comment.\n- The repair keeps every case. The fixture `usable()` now supplies a synthetic register, because CUT-A replaced the example's register with placeholders. The S1 owner case uses the same register. The first case changes its expectation for the example file: it now stops on a missing register as well as a missing version, and it passes only when both are filled. That is a stronger check on the example. It weakens no assertion about production behavior and changes no deadline. The case-correspondence record shows 204 cases before and after, none added and none missing, and one renamed title.\n- The follow-up at d19e9453 ran the compiler of `examples/repo-in-ai`, pool compatibility, the whole owning file (204 of 204 passed) and the unreached Native stage with scale cases (1,155 passed, 2 skipped, 6 scale cases passed, exit 0, 1,318 s).\n\nWhat I read:\n\n- `scripts/register-values.mjs`. It validates the complete candidate with the production parsers (`readInstalledRegisters`, `artifactsConfiguration`, `demoCreationConfig`, `smokePolicy`) before it writes. It refuses a dirty target, a file that differs from HEAD, and a file that changes during preparation. It edits only `REGISTER_SCOPE`, `ARTIFACTS_CONFIG`, `INSTALLED_REGISTER_SCOPES` and `DEMO_START_CONFIG`, and it never adds `DEPLOYMENT`. The span reader refuses duplicate keys.\n- The config diffs. `wrangler.demo.jsonc` and `wrangler.artroom-scope.jsonc` change comments only. No register value changes in this head.\n- The tests. `demo-config.test.ts` and `deploy-smoke.test.mjs` read the identities from the tracked files instead of copying them. `register-values.test.mjs` joins `nodeFiles` in `scripts/test.mjs`.\n- `docs/deploy.md`. Its claim that the client accepts Register 28 offers holds (`packages/client/src/creation-offer.ts:20`).\n\nWhat I checked:\n\n- Scope. Main 694a8c7f is an ancestor, and the pushed branch equals the head. The head changes 22 paths, and each has an artifact at the head.\n- Evidence. The four manifests hash to 44ba0113, 61f4d89c, 4c336ee0 and d45c76ff, as the request states. All 124 listed files match their SHA-256 and byte counts, and none is missing. `SHA256SUMS` verifies in all five directories. The gate's `head.txt` names 554187d4 and tree 7f7e180f, and the follow-up's names d19e9453 and tree 4327b264. All 13 gate samples and all 67 follow-up samples read AC Power, and powermode is 0 at each start and end. The host's `pmset -g log` shows no sleep or wake from 01:00 to 03:00 EST.\n- Cheap checks. The commit-message check passes: 8 checked, 0 flagged. `git diff --check` is clean. I ran no tests, because Head A holds the slot.\n\nArchitecture: sound. The tracked file stays the one source of a Worker's register settings, and the helper reuses the hosted-name map and the production parsers instead of a second map. Head A becomes the output of one command for each Worker.\n\nSecurity: no finding. The helper reads and writes public configuration only, it reads no secret, and it checks an explicit `--deployment` against the Start offer instead of tracking `DEPLOYMENT`. Two notes